# =============================================================================
# HotelERP — configuration index
# =============================================================================
# There is NO shared root .env. Each deployable unit owns its own env file:
#
#   Backend — one .env PER SERVICE, self-contained (DB, secrets, CORS, URLs):
#     Backend/Services/LoginServices/.env
#     Backend/Services/UserServices/.env
#     Backend/Services/MasterDataServices/.env
#     Backend/Services/HotelServices/.env
#     Backend/Services/RestaurantServices/.env
#     Backend/Services/BarServices/.env
#   Template + full contract:  Backend/Services/.env.example
#
#   Frontend — Frontend/.env        (template: Frontend/.env.example)
#
# Each service loads ONLY its own .env (configs/__init__.py). start-network.ps1
# reads each service's SERVICE_HOST/SERVICE_PORT to launch it.
#
# CRITICAL: JWT_SECRET_KEY, SESSION_SECRET and JWT_ISSUER MUST be identical in
# every service's .env, or every authenticated request returns 401.
# =============================================================================
